 ### [Contour Rendering Shading](8315-contour-rendering-shading.md)
-is a view-dependent shading technique that highlights object surfaces by weighting ray samples based on the alignment between the view vector and the surface gradient. It solves the problem of visualizing distinct structural boundaries in volume data where conventional opacity transfer functions fail. Unlike standard shading methods that rely on lighting models, it produces a non-photorealistic line-art effect maximized when the view direction is tangent to the surface. Choose it when rendering contour-based visualizations or when structural boundaries need emphasis over photorealism.
